{
 "format": "tethercorkboard",
 "version": 1,
 "board": {
  "id": "example-research-web",
  "name": "Example: cooling a city (a web of linked ideas)",
  "items": [
   {
    "text": "Start here. Follow the strings from causes, to effects, to what we could do about them.",
    "parentId": null,
    "id": "goal",
    "kind": "note",
    "x": 1210,
    "y": -330,
    "w": 320,
    "h": 190,
    "title": "How do we keep our city cooler?",
    "color": "#e6d4ff",
    "typeId": "type-question",
    "fields": {
     "question-status": "Researching"
    }
   },
   {
    "text": "",
    "parentId": null,
    "id": "causes",
    "kind": "section",
    "x": 0,
    "y": 0,
    "w": 920,
    "h": 700,
    "title": "Causes",
    "color": "#c9eab8",
    "typeId": "type-topic",
    "fields": {
     "topic-summary": "Why a city runs hotter than the countryside around it."
    }
   },
   {
    "text": "",
    "parentId": null,
    "id": "effects",
    "kind": "section",
    "x": 1000,
    "y": 0,
    "w": 920,
    "h": 700,
    "title": "Effects",
    "color": "#ffd0dc",
    "typeId": "type-topic",
    "fields": {
     "topic-summary": "What the extra heat does to people and the city."
    }
   },
   {
    "text": "",
    "parentId": null,
    "id": "solutions",
    "kind": "section",
    "x": 2000,
    "y": 0,
    "w": 920,
    "h": 700,
    "title": "Solutions",
    "color": "#c6e2ff",
    "typeId": "type-topic",
    "fields": {
     "topic-summary": "Things a city can change to bring temperatures down."
    }
   },
   {
    "text": "Asphalt and dark roofs soak up sunlight and give it back as heat.",
    "parentId": "causes",
    "id": "c-dark",
    "kind": "note",
    "title": "Dark surfaces",
    "color": "#fff4a3",
    "typeId": "type-claim",
    "fields": {
     "claim-confidence": "High"
    },
    "x": 30,
    "y": 90,
    "w": 250,
    "h": 160
   },
   {
    "text": "Fewer plants and trees means less shade and less cooling from evaporation.",
    "parentId": "causes",
    "id": "c-green",
    "kind": "note",
    "title": "Less vegetation",
    "color": "#fff4a3",
    "typeId": "type-claim",
    "fields": {
     "claim-confidence": "High"
    },
    "x": 310,
    "y": 90,
    "w": 250,
    "h": 160
   },
   {
    "text": "Air conditioners, vehicles and industry release heat straight into the air.",
    "parentId": "causes",
    "id": "c-waste",
    "kind": "note",
    "title": "Waste heat",
    "color": "#fff4a3",
    "typeId": "type-claim",
    "fields": {
     "claim-confidence": "Medium"
    },
    "x": 590,
    "y": 90,
    "w": 250,
    "h": 160
   },
   {
    "text": "Tall buildings and narrow streets slow the wind and hold heat in.",
    "parentId": "causes",
    "id": "c-canyon",
    "kind": "note",
    "title": "Street canyons",
    "color": "#fff4a3",
    "typeId": "type-claim",
    "fields": {
     "claim-confidence": "Medium"
    },
    "x": 30,
    "y": 280,
    "w": 250,
    "h": 160
   },
   {
    "text": "Our city may not match the general picture.",
    "parentId": "causes",
    "id": "q-share",
    "kind": "note",
    "title": "How much is each cause worth here?",
    "color": "#ffd0dc",
    "typeId": "type-question",
    "fields": {
     "question-status": "Open"
    },
    "x": 310,
    "y": 280,
    "w": 250,
    "h": 160
   },
   {
    "text": "More air conditioning on hot days pushes demand up.",
    "parentId": "effects",
    "id": "e-energy",
    "kind": "note",
    "title": "Higher energy use",
    "color": "#fff4a3",
    "typeId": "type-claim",
    "fields": {
     "claim-confidence": "High"
    },
    "x": 1030,
    "y": 90,
    "w": 250,
    "h": 160
   },
   {
    "text": "The city stays warmer after sunset than nearby countryside, so there is less time to cool off.",
    "parentId": "effects",
    "id": "e-nights",
    "kind": "note",
    "title": "Hot nights",
    "color": "#fff4a3",
    "typeId": "type-claim",
    "fields": {
     "claim-confidence": "High"
    },
    "x": 1310,
    "y": 90,
    "w": 250,
    "h": 160
   },
   {
    "text": "Long hot spells with no cool night are hardest on older people and young children.",
    "parentId": "effects",
    "id": "e-health",
    "kind": "note",
    "title": "Heat illness",
    "color": "#fff4a3",
    "typeId": "type-claim",
    "fields": {
     "claim-confidence": "High"
    },
    "x": 1590,
    "y": 90,
    "w": 250,
    "h": 160
   },
   {
    "text": "Heat speeds up the chemistry that makes smog.",
    "parentId": "effects",
    "id": "e-smog",
    "kind": "note",
    "title": "Worse air quality",
    "color": "#fff4a3",
    "typeId": "type-claim",
    "fields": {
     "claim-confidence": "Medium"
    },
    "x": 1030,
    "y": 280,
    "w": 250,
    "h": 160
   },
   {
    "text": "Probably those with the least shade.",
    "parentId": "effects",
    "id": "q-where",
    "kind": "note",
    "title": "Which neighbourhoods are hit hardest?",
    "color": "#ffd0dc",
    "typeId": "type-question",
    "fields": {
     "question-status": "Open"
    },
    "x": 1310,
    "y": 280,
    "w": 250,
    "h": 160
   },
   {
    "text": "Shade and evaporation cool the street, and they last for decades.",
    "parentId": "solutions",
    "id": "s-trees",
    "kind": "note",
    "title": "Street trees",
    "color": "#fff4a3",
    "typeId": "type-claim",
    "fields": {
     "claim-confidence": "High"
    },
    "x": 2030,
    "y": 90,
    "w": 250,
    "h": 160
   },
   {
    "text": "Light-coloured roofs reflect sunlight instead of absorbing it.",
    "parentId": "solutions",
    "id": "s-coolroof",
    "kind": "note",
    "title": "Cool roofs",
    "color": "#fff4a3",
    "typeId": "type-claim",
    "fields": {
     "claim-confidence": "High"
    },
    "x": 2310,
    "y": 90,
    "w": 250,
    "h": 160
   },
   {
    "text": "Plants on a roof insulate the building and cool the air above it.",
    "parentId": "solutions",
    "id": "s-greenroof",
    "kind": "note",
    "title": "Green roofs",
    "color": "#fff4a3",
    "typeId": "type-claim",
    "fields": {
     "claim-confidence": "Medium"
    },
    "x": 2590,
    "y": 90,
    "w": 250,
    "h": 160
   },
   {
    "text": "Pale road and path surfaces stay cooler in the sun.",
    "parentId": "solutions",
    "id": "s-pave",
    "kind": "note",
    "title": "Lighter pavements",
    "color": "#fff4a3",
    "typeId": "type-claim",
    "fields": {
     "claim-confidence": "Medium"
    },
    "x": 2030,
    "y": 280,
    "w": 250,
    "h": 160
   },
   {
    "text": "Open green space and fountains give people places to cool down.",
    "parentId": "solutions",
    "id": "s-parks",
    "kind": "note",
    "title": "Parks and water",
    "color": "#fff4a3",
    "typeId": "type-claim",
    "fields": {
     "claim-confidence": "Medium"
    },
    "x": 2310,
    "y": 280,
    "w": 250,
    "h": 160
   },
   {
    "text": "Compare cost against how many people each option helps.",
    "parentId": "solutions",
    "id": "q-afford",
    "kind": "note",
    "title": "What can we afford first?",
    "color": "#ffd0dc",
    "typeId": "type-question",
    "fields": {
     "question-status": "Researching"
    },
    "x": 2590,
    "y": 280,
    "w": 250,
    "h": 160
   },
   {
    "text": "",
    "parentId": null,
